on "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{6}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/41/4177d9520b3758b29926eba7a7a74ed4c508d861e3c343f46c372ec79500fc9d.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note that for $x>1$, the graph grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ \n\nWe say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, there are no horizontal asymptotes." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-37ad94da-747c-5f20-8c1e-e2c0668e7607"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37ad94da-747c-5f20-8c1e-e2c0668e7607" :answer-field/id #uuid "37ad94da-747c-5f20-8c1e-e2c0668e7607" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-14c52374-9b9f-5ea2-9b1d-640924d6082b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c6d8c85-9923-5fdb-8597-d5d5d1259719" "answer-a4afd188-4d20-517e-a47b-c6882d781b67" "answer-44521491-c131-5639-a63c-726e10f92842" "answer-7569d322-3718-5d60-86d6-93dea8795fd0" "answer-14c52374-9b9f-5ea2-9b1d-640924d6082b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c6d8c85-9923-5fdb-8597-d5d5d1259719" :answer/id #uuid "5c6d8c85-9923-5fdb-8597-d5d5d1259719" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4afd188-4d20-517e-a47b-c6882d781b67" :answer/id #uuid "a4afd188-4d20-517e-a47b-c6882d781b67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44521491-c131-5639-a63c-726e10f92842" :answer/id #uuid "44521491-c131-5639-a63c-726e10f92842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7569d322-3718-5d60-86d6-93dea8795fd0" :answer/id #uuid "7569d322-3718-5d60-86d6-93dea8795fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14c52374-9b9f-5ea2-9b1d-640924d6082b" :answer/id #uuid "14c52374-9b9f-5ea2-9b1d-640924d6082b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no horizontal asymptotes." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111382 :question/problem "Which of the following is a zero of $y={log}_{5}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{5}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f0/f095d09fd04a982ad51ff3859f6d789083ed7528b382457954e45cf259cc06a5.png)\n\nNote that the graph passes through the point $(1,0).$ \n\nTherefore, the zero of the function $y={log}_{5}⁡x$ is $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110017 :answer-field/correct "answer-c52bc628-e221-5ead-8655-971a0094fb2d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-967407a3-388d-50e5-b05f-6024104a481d" "answer-3434375c-1ed2-5f71-80ef-9421d3daba23" "answer-c52bc628-e221-5ead-8655-971a0094fb2d" "answer-772a545f-c998-5cca-b0ca-b27d118ff58d" "answer-82d33dd7-17dd-5d35-859e-346211ae4641"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-967407a3-388d-50e5-b05f-6024104a481d" :answer/id #uuid "967407a3-388d-50e5-b05f-6024104a481d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3434375c-1ed2-5f71-80ef-9421d3daba23" :answer/id #uuid "3434375c-1ed2-5f71-80ef-9421d3daba23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c52bc628-e221-5ead-8655-971a0094fb2d" :answer/id #uuid "c52bc628-e221-5ead-8655-971a0094fb2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-772a545f-c998-5cca-b0ca-b27d118ff58d" :answer/id #uuid "772a545f-c998-5cca-b0ca-b27d118ff58d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82d33dd7-17dd-5d35-859e-346211ae4641" :answer/id #uuid "82d33dd7-17dd-5d35-859e-346211ae4641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111219 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x?$\n\nI. The function passes through the point $(1,0)$\n\nII. Its horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$\n\nIII. It passes through the point $(10,100).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/17/177d2949118515d96b6a1c49d0222a2417ab6236e8641f8d89c0cd8f6b30a592.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x$ has no horizontal asymptote. However, it does have the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Substituting $x=10$ into the equation of the curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(10) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1}) \\\\  & =1\\ne 100\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186109039 :answer-field/correct 17592186109041 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233519 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{6}⁡x?$ \n\nI. It has no zeros\n\nII. $y\\to 6$ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\nIII. It has a vertical asymptote at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{6}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/d8/d8d3f9dc995d8801d451b15129860362efa772178cdc3ef07be5adb6a1da5c45.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a zero at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As $x$ increases, $y$ increases without bound. Therefore, $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true." :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b179eeb3-b9e7-569b-a20d-09ef65081dfe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b179eeb3-b9e7-569b-a20d-09ef65081dfe" :answer-field/id #uuid "b179eeb3-b9e7-569b-a20d-09ef65081dfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2d1effa9-7e1a-55a3-81d4-aac75787131d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9334f19-c8ae-5204-a395-20c07315d341" "answer-dd5aa106-d5f2-58b4-962e-4d9b7feff98e" "answer-5963bb65-6486-5a51-a43b-a6e3dcb86561" "answer-0b0f5b8f-e5e0-519d-aa21-ccb7de143a67" "answer-2d1effa9-7e1a-55a3-81d4-aac75787131d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9334f19-c8ae-5204-a395-20c07315d341" :answer/id #uuid "d9334f19-c8ae-5204-a395-20c07315d341" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd5aa106-d5f2-58b4-962e-4d9b7feff98e" :answer/id #uuid "dd5aa106-d5f2-58b4-962e-4d9b7feff98e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5963bb65-6486-5a51-a43b-a6e3dcb86561" :answer/id #uuid "5963bb65-6486-5a51-a43b-a6e3dcb86561" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b0f5b8f-e5e0-519d-aa21-ccb7de143a67" :answer/id #uuid "0b0f5b8f-e5e0-519d-aa21-ccb7de143a67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d1effa9-7e1a-55a3-81d4-aac75787131d" :answer/id #uuid "2d1effa9-7e1a-55a3-81d4-aac75787131d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-96d6c320-22a1-578b-bc1b-575bf1a1c004" :question/id #uuid "96d6c320-22a1-578b-bc1b-575bf1a1c004" :question/math-academy-id "q-156742" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{8}⁡x?$\n\nI. The domain is $x\\ge 0$\n\nII. It has no horizontal asymptotes\n\nIII. It passes through the point $(64,2)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{8}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/68/6811e57f1259b97448811ac9abe8d6fc7f76a52b62e685f2fa0ec36e290381b4.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, we see that the domain is $x>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $y={log}_{8}⁡x$ has no horizontal asymptote. However, it does have the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Substituting $x=64$ into the equation of the curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{8}⁡(64) \\\\  & ={log}_{8}⁡({8}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{log}_{8}⁡(8) \\\\  & =2\\,\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements II and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c42bbbe5-1f49-507b-a85b-15a0a5e80a99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c42bbbe5-1f49-507b-a85b-15a0a5e80a99" :answer-field/id #uuid "c42bbbe5-1f49-507b-a85b-15a0a5e80a99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-62e95736-ac92-5898-8904-f57247321448" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f270d552-6c79-5d29-8e6a-1213fad5b8b7" "answer-eff2370c-3b33-5e79-a285-16c3e0abb4ba" "answer-c5b8c9e5-0db3-58d3-ac01-f00cd2950bda" "answer-62e95736-ac92-5898-8904-f57247321448" "answer-834c2010-d5e2-594b-8783-23e8ef44ba8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f270d552-6c79-5d29-8e6a-1213fad5b8b7" :answer/id #uuid "f270d552-6c79-5d29-8e6a-1213fad5b8b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eff2370c-3b33-5e79-a285-16c3e0abb4ba" :answer/id #uuid "eff2370c-3b33-5e79-a285-16c3e0abb4ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5b8c9e5-0db3-58d3-ac01-f00cd2950bda" :answer/id #uuid "c5b8c9e5-0db3-58d3-ac01-f00cd2950bda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62e95736-ac92-5898-8904-f57247321448" :answer/id #uuid "62e95736-ac92-5898-8904-f57247321448" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-834c2010-d5e2-594b-8783-23e8ef44ba8b" :answer/id #uuid "834c2010-d5e2-594b-8783-23e8ef44ba8b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111907 :tutorial/content "To plot the graph of a logarithmic function, it helps to remember that the inverse of a logarithmic function is an exponential function. So, we can just plot the exponential function and reflect it over the line $y=x.$\n\nFor example, suppose that we wish to plot the graph of \n\n$$\ny=\\log_2 x.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding inverse function is $y=2^x,$ and since $y=2^x$ is a one-to-one function defined for all real $x,$ we can obtain the graph of $y=\\log_2{x}$ by reflecting $y=2^x$ over the line $y=x.$ The result is shown below:\n\n![](images/0c/0c614201798324262429f080d8e8a31bfefe58c4008bfe82e6da1b91dc158b7a.png)\n\nHere are some key points to note about $y=\\log_2(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n- The domain is $x>0$, and the range is $-\\infty <   y <   \\infty.$\n\n- The graph has the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- The function is an increasing function.\n\n- The graph passes through the point $(1,0).$\n\n- For $x>1$, the graph is positive and grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ We say that $y\\rightarrow \\infty$ (slowly) as $x\\rightarrow \\infty.$\n\nIn general, for any base $n>1,$ the graph of $y=\\log_n{x}$ always has the same shape, and all of the above points are valid. We can verify that this is true by inspecting some possible graphs shown below:\n\n![](images/91/91567f282acbc3b8390da1e4147b445018ae649d913205e59867d58ea980ff7b.png)\n\n**Note:** The important points covered above also apply to two familiar logarithms.\n\n- $y = \\ln x = \\log_e x$ is the natural logarithm. Since the base is $n=e>1,$ all of the important points covered above apply.\n\n- $y = \\log x = \\log_{10} x$ is the logarithm with base $10.$ Since the base is $n=10>1,$ all the important points covered above apply." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110877 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054604 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d591e3b7-0993-5fb9-b7f0-ff97c33bf559" "question-2b9acb7e-8235-5df0-907d-863119079541"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d591e3b7-0993-5fb9-b7f0-ff97c33bf559" :question/id #uuid "d591e3b7-0993-5fb9-b7f0-ff97c33bf559" :question/math-academy-id "q-100250" :question/problem "Find ${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt[3]{2{x}^{4}-5}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt[3]{2{x}^{4}-5}}=\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 2}3x}{{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt[3]{2{x}^{4}-5}}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\nFor the numerator, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}3x & =3{lim}_{x\\to 2}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the root rule in the denominator, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt[3]{2{x}^{4}-5} & =\\sqrt[3]{{lim}_{x\\to 2}(2{x}^{4}-5)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{2(2)^{4}-5)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{27} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt[3]{2{x}^{4}-5}} & =\\frac{6}{3}=2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ddff0f96-aeb7-5490-8d56-4c8b9d0de231"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ddff0f96-aeb7-5490-8d56-4c8b9d0de231" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddff0f96-aeb7-5490-8d56-4c8b9d0de231" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff7f4802-e1a5-55e2-9352-05637b9f8392" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff7f4802-e1a5-55e2-9352-05637b9f8392" "answer-a0bf2b88-34c6-53e4-a455-89e06f7f9a7a" "answer-16ba1e29-25ac-579d-9cfe-24448c56edab" "answer-fbdaaac8-b49f-51b4-b323-7ea59a4fdd9d" "answer-db467dc8-4b26-512d-821f-e3c4973e9fd6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff7f4802-e1a5-55e2-9352-05637b9f8392" :answer/id #uuid "ff7f4802-e1a5-55e2-9352-05637b9f8392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0bf2b88-34c6-53e4-a455-89e06f7f9a7a" :answer/id #uuid "a0bf2b88-34c6-53e4-a455-89e06f7f9a7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16ba1e29-25ac-579d-9cfe-24448c56edab" :answer/id #uuid "16ba1e29-25ac-579d-9cfe-24448c56edab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbdaaac8-b49f-51b4-b323-7ea59a4fdd9d" :answer/id #uuid "fbdaaac8-b49f-51b4-b323-7ea59a4fdd9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db467dc8-4b26-512d-821f-e3c4973e9fd6" :answer/id #uuid "db467dc8-4b26-512d-821f-e3c4973e9fd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054703 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-41ad1c03-af11-5517-b3f9-c73f27dc13ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-41ad1c03-af11-5517-b3f9-c73f27dc13ff" :question/id #uuid "41ad1c03-af11-5517-b3f9-c73f27dc13ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-338364" :question/problem "![](images/94/94027c25ef78ae46d0deb4b577339daf878efd71b71029a9575f9c8ed9096e2c.png)\n\nIf the figure above shows the graph of the function $f(x),$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x-1)^{2}\\,(f(x)-2)^{3}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=3.$\n\nFrom the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x-1)^{2}\\,(f(x)-2)^{3}={lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x-1)^{2}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(f(x)-2)^{3}.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of each factor, separately.\n\nApplying the power rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x-1)^{2} & ={({lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x-1))}^{2} \\\\  & =(2-1)^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(f(x)-2)^{3} & ={({lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(f(x)-2))}^{3} \\\\  & =(3-2)^{3} \\\\  & ={1}^{3} \\\\  & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,2}(x-1)^{2}\\,(f(x)-2)^{3} & =(1)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-817fc64f-fe17-5ab1-8ab5-8f8ebfd722a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-817fc64f-fe17-5ab1-8ab5-8f8ebfd722a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "817fc64f-fe17-5ab1-8ab5-8f8ebfd722a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-066cb984-e17a-5fea-af4c-48188475d862" :answer-field/choices ["answer-066cb984-e17a-5fea-af4c-48188475d862"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-066cb984-e17a-5fea-af4c-48188475d862" :answer/id #uuid "066cb984-e17a-5fea-af4c-48188475d862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2b9acb7e-8235-5df0-907d-863119079541" :question/id #uuid "2b9acb7e-8235-5df0-907d-863119079541" :question/math-academy-id "q-338390" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the limit.\n\n${lim}_{t\\to -1}(\\sqrt[7]{(2t+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{({t}^{2}+t+1)^{6}})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the sum and root rules, we get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to -1}(\\sqrt[7]{(2t+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{({t}^{2}+t+1)^{6}}) & ={lim}_{t\\to -1}\\sqrt[7]{(2t+1)^{7}}-{lim}_{t\\to -1}\\sqrt[3]{({t}^{2}+t+1)^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{{({lim}_{t\\to -1}(2t+1))}^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{{({lim}_{t\\to -1}({t}^{2}+t+1))}^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{(2(-1)+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{(((-1)^{2}+(-1)+1))^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{(-2+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{((1-1+1))^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{(-1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{(1)^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{-1}-\\sqrt[3]{1} \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32d33a71-45d3-5a70-b6f2-f587f0b3ec0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32d33a71-45d3-5a70-b6f2-f587f0b3ec0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "32d33a71-45d3-5a70-b6f2-f587f0b3ec0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0d434ed0-8529-5bae-a087-2963bb7442d3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d434ed0-8529-5bae-a087-2963bb7442d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d434ed0-8529-5bae-a087-2963bb7442d3" :answer/id #uuid "0d434ed0-8529-5bae-a087-2963bb7442d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-893cd585-763a-5ad4-9659-5052de0c1e02" :activity/id #uuid "893cd585-763a-5ad4-9659-5052de0c1e02" :activity/title "The Power and Root Rules for Limits" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050987 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-2e1eff63-f8c6-5d02-9662-7565ab1c3899" "step-9a7d063a-cc3c-5001-8da3-bc7d18a9ea75" "step-75c9d97b-2b75-5de2-b1d4-d07fb1dfbf30"] :activity/first-step "step-2e1eff63-f8c6-5d02-9662-7565ab1c3899" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2e1eff63-f8c6-5d02-9662-7565ab1c3899" :step/id #uuid "2e1eff63-f8c6-5d02-9662-7565ab1c3899" :step/content "question-d591e3b7-0993-5fb9-b7f0-ff97c33bf559" :step/next "step-9a7d063a-cc3c-5001-8da3-bc7d18a9ea75" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9a7d063a-cc3c-5001-8da3-bc7d18a9ea75" :step/id #uuid "9a7d063a-cc3c-5001-8da3-bc7d18a9ea75" :step/content "question-41ad1c03-af11-5517-b3f9-c73f27dc13ff" :step/next "step-75c9d97b-2b75-5de2-b1d4-d07fb1dfbf30" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-75c9d97b-2b75-5de2-b1d4-d07fb1dfbf30" :step/id #uuid "75c9d97b-2b75-5de2-b1d4-d07fb1dfbf30" :step/content "question-2b9acb7e-8235-5df0-907d-863119079541" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191120] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191121] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191117] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191118] [:db/retract 17592186191116 :answer-field/choices 17592186191119] {:db/id 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" "question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193178 :question/problem "![](images/c2/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/id #uuid "e603e7ce-cd31-56e2-8f70-d962ee5aba80" :question/math-academy-id "q-161587" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/51/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=1-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=1-x\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/id #uuid "384c0059-ce47-5e74-b060-3765aa340bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" "answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" "answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" "answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/id #uuid "13fd9d33-1bbf-5c4c-9405-5a13f110f97a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y<1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/id #uuid "84c46602-c418-55b4-8c8c-fe9fb64de61d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/id #uuid "00eb3ffb-cab6-5207-a9b5-44c32f9da60c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y>1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/id #uuid "116943d6-eb2d-55e6-9dda-aafbd2ea63e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\ge 1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/id #uuid "2c257415-8128-5ecd-8dee-4d4626ceb5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\le 1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193205 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b0c3e30fcb7e748a80cdf98892291599967151343efe671aca790b2528039c4c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186191116 :answer-field/correct "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer-field/choices ["answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" "answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" "answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" "answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/id #uuid "02df4ca7-40fc-58de-9931-ef11c4168884" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/id #uuid "7c441582-fa30-574b-8ce8-6196d8d8e742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/id #uuid "2c3fa36b-e7b4-5168-89e5-5493708f6246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/id #uuid "4040d25f-bc45-504f-baac-b4dd1af89e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/id #uuid "e4cdb40d-25b4-51cb-891c-ebd4165f234b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186378836 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2+x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/ac2b2f009daf16725be7d3a00743a1d1b75b437b936026fa2be898d94c8c93b4.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2+x\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/id #uuid "3c4b52d1-eec1-5fd6-92e3-909a0fe3f144" :question/math-academy-id "q-161586" :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/c2/c2b4e3d11f16920ce24a279289808d3f5dc4e68563525f1417c8767a5446b461.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\,\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3055df-25f1-51fb-b6a5-e5fcf68dc1a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" "answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" "answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" "answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/id #uuid "e8bc646a-6ed6-567d-91b1-5937398d3b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/id #uuid "ff68216f-d4cb-5463-b5ce-1c0632a5bd8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/id #uuid "8a83a6ae-3b5d-5339-8b54-d04f55d02bf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/id #uuid "fc00b173-ef2f-52a6-a3ba-e417d3948649" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/id #uuid "f08d22b4-e18a-5abd-b464-4106187ad8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281303 :question/problem "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186379973 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/40/4073e99607c1e824f67b24bc93955b39c5b320901cd391ff3adb51444d1e1416.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/79/79e005cc03bb625657c652324db58db653882c640e94ea4b21a386676745bd14.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<-x\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186407107 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0\\le y<2\\}\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71851a12f638da9604450cae0d50ed15187e850368890845d60b16b89e728bcf.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/abdd434da59bb3a1bdc0ee7de398d7ea4aeae2f617f54b5a26a5bad871ba0ac4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2\\,\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193324 :question/problem "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y<0\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281306 :question/problem "![](images/6d/6debac35386e085a0197cf9eb3f2da65cc719ace67163cad625f58c056fb8f67.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179764 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a056777d-2d90-5391-b8e4-3c8ae89bd6c6" "question-aceecb75-92cf-58b4-997d-d31ecad9d81f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a056777d-2d90-5391-b8e4-3c8ae89bd6c6" :question/id #uuid "a056777d-2d90-5391-b8e4-3c8ae89bd6c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-4064" :question/problem "$3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{27}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}=$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{27}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{5}} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{4}\\cdot x} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{x}^{4}}\\cdot \\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{3}-3\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ (3-3)\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 0\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c61d8497-db30-5312-b6cc-cc9f8eeed283"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c61d8497-db30-5312-b6cc-cc9f8eeed283" :answer-field/id #uuid "c61d8497-db30-5312-b6cc-cc9f8eeed283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" "answer-ebcfccec-dd55-5089-ac9a-b0ae93280f1a" "answer-9026f5ff-791a-5770-911f-0b0b83b85fb1" "answer-ac5245bd-caba-5f74-b81d-55f9a9e8ac2d" "answer-9c93eb0d-6ded-596d-b4ab-b36cd01140e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer/id #uuid "85b4904a-d133-59e2-89df-d49b787f7a62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebcfccec-dd55-5089-ac9a-b0ae93280f1a" :answer/id #uuid "ebcfccec-dd55-5089-ac9a-b0ae93280f1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{3{x}^{2}-{x}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9026f5ff-791a-5770-911f-0b0b83b85fb1" :answer/id #uuid "9026f5ff-791a-5770-911f-0b0b83b85fb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-3x\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac5245bd-caba-5f74-b81d-55f9a9e8ac2d" :answer/id #uuid "ac5245bd-caba-5f74-b81d-55f9a9e8ac2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-x\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c93eb0d-6ded-596d-b4ab-b36cd01140e1" :answer/id #uuid "9c93eb0d-6ded-596d-b4ab-b36cd01140e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}-{x}^{2}\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179751 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ce532f1b-ce31-55ab-8ca6-180ef8818c5e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ce532f1b-ce31-55ab-8ca6-180ef8818c5e" :question/id #uuid "ce532f1b-ce31-55ab-8ca6-180ef8818c5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-29319" :question/problem "Simplify $3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, and the two $\\sqrt{y}$ terms together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt[3]{y}-4\\sqrt{y}-7\\sqrt[3]{y}+2\\sqrt{y} & = \\\\ (-4+2)\\sqrt{y}+(3-7)\\sqrt[3]{y} & = \\\\ -2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8669faa-71b0-532d-ba32-5f961f40b158"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8669faa-71b0-532d-ba32-5f961f40b158" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8669faa-71b0-532d-ba32-5f961f40b158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1aed403b-dbdf-50cf-b8cc-99506a344078" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1aed403b-dbdf-50cf-b8cc-99506a344078" "answer-0c2f4616-54cd-5516-be79-b77cd37a59b2" "answer-89462c96-0fb9-5051-8f94-3c90423306ca" "answer-784a2285-292b-5a35-aaf7-7340d809529b" "answer-40bbda36-b2ef-5389-b981-78447392ad16"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1aed403b-dbdf-50cf-b8cc-99506a344078" :answer/id #uuid "1aed403b-dbdf-50cf-b8cc-99506a344078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c2f4616-54cd-5516-be79-b77cd37a59b2" :answer/id #uuid "0c2f4616-54cd-5516-be79-b77cd37a59b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\sqrt{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89462c96-0fb9-5051-8f94-3c90423306ca" :answer/id #uuid "89462c96-0fb9-5051-8f94-3c90423306ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{y}-5\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-784a2285-292b-5a35-aaf7-7340d809529b" :answer/id #uuid "784a2285-292b-5a35-aaf7-7340d809529b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{y}-4\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40bbda36-b2ef-5389-b981-78447392ad16" :answer/id #uuid "40bbda36-b2ef-5389-b981-78447392ad16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{y}-2\\sqrt[3]{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-aceecb75-92cf-58b4-997d-d31ecad9d81f" :question/id #uuid "aceecb75-92cf-58b4-997d-d31ecad9d81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29322" :question/problem "Simplify $2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\sqrt{54}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9\\cdot 6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 2x\\cdot 3\\cdot \\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ 6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}-5x\\sqrt{6} & = \\\\ (6x-5x)\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2edd54bc-8785-50e5-9005-f3528fdfbcbc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2edd54bc-8785-50e5-9005-f3528fdfbcbc" :answer-field/id #uuid "2edd54bc-8785-50e5-9005-f3528fdfbcbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18d7d654-83a6-5095-8350-0c24ed3b09f3" "answer-3f460124-51cf-5f31-ae09-245b7c4d361f" "answer-5b0c664c-f8c9-5f53-b9f0-e91c57fa6455" "answer-8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" "answer-e8fc2ea4-ed54-5789-9c1b-da6da0a36fc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18d7d654-83a6-5095-8350-0c24ed3b09f3" :answer/id #uuid "18d7d654-83a6-5095-8350-0c24ed3b09f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f460124-51cf-5f31-ae09-245b7c4d361f" :answer/id #uuid "3f460124-51cf-5f31-ae09-245b7c4d361f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b0c664c-f8c9-5f53-b9f0-e91c57fa6455" :answer/id #uuid "5b0c664c-f8c9-5f53-b9f0-e91c57fa6455" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer/id #uuid "8d383985-681c-53c8-9484-5c98b6262456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}+2x\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8fc2ea4-ed54-5789-9c1b-da6da0a36fc2" :answer/id #uuid "e8fc2ea4-ed54-5789-9c1b-da6da0a36fc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\sqrt{6}-x\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5f674834-2a57-5e4c-9972-af563d469b92" :activity/id #uuid "5f674834-2a57-5e4c-9972-af563d469b92" :activity/title "Adding and Subtracting Radical Expressions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048138 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-8968f935-7b70-53c6-a08f-fcaf88c8bc02" "step-749f734f-f9f3-581f-9e6b-58c70b1f490a" "step-b609203c-4095-58fb-bb8f-2ece8932910b"] :activity/first-step "step-8968f935-7b70-53c6-a08f-fcaf88c8bc02" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-8968f935-7b70-53c6-a08f-fcaf88c8bc02" :step/id #uuid "8968f935-7b70-53c6-a08f-fcaf88c8bc02" :step/content "question-a056777d-2d90-5391-b8e4-3c8ae89bd6c6" :step/next "step-749f734f-f9f3-581f-9e6b-58c70b1f490a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-749f734f-f9f3-581f-9e6b-58c70b1f490a" :step/id #uuid "749f734f-f9f3-581f-9e6b-58c70b1f490a" :step/content "question-ce532f1b-ce31-55ab-8ca6-180ef8818c5e" :step/next "step-b609203c-4095-58fb-bb8f-2ece8932910b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b609203c-4095-58fb-bb8f-2ece8932910b" :step/id #uuid "b609203c-4095-58fb-bb8f-2ece8932910b" :step/content "question-aceecb75-92cf-58b4-997d-d31ecad9d81f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078393 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b2b55850-322e-5b17-9a94-b2696bd083f6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078737 :question/problem "![](images/d0/d04a8e993da8e90ca75f5f7541317d26a6a9c8f9b76cdb9c95511080035177c5.png)\n\nFind the cosine of $∠Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the definition of cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡Y=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac{XY}{YZ}=\\frac{XY}{5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $XY.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{Y{Z}^{2}-X{Z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}-(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25-7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡Y & =\\frac{XY}{5}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075298 :answer-field/correct 17592186075301 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2b55850-322e-5b17-9a94-b2696bd083f6" :question/id #uuid "b2b55850-322e-5b17-9a94-b2696bd083f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-122050" :question/problem "In the right triangle $△JKL,$ $∠J$ is a right angle, $JL=8$ and $KL=12.$ Find $\\operatorname{tan}⁡K.$" :question/worked-solution "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](images/cc/cc33327cc6d071cb6ec9ac0c10d58e57bc35f8d81b326731120cf04c18f58ec1.png)\n\nRecall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡K=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{JL}{JK}=\\frac{8}{JK}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $JK.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}JK & =\\sqrt{K{L}^{2}-J{L}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡K & =\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f15bdbe8-d486-594d-b02d-d29460c4afc4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f15bdbe8-d486-594d-b02d-d29460c4afc4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f15bdbe8-d486-594d-b02d-d29460c4afc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-35b1eb42-ba69-53f4-81c2-c8740d0d9806" :answer-field/choices ["answer-493e3c85-b25e-53b6-a08c-4fea9dba4c1c" "answer-35b1eb42-ba69-53f4-81c2-c8740d0d9806" "answer-2561f127-b662-5797-b919-80264e333b26" "answer-c48feefc-15c4-5bef-ac32-e7d9d07bb0ce" "answer-d04f3cfc-1715-5df0-995f-34492b52003c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-493e3c85-b25e-53b6-a08c-4fea9dba4c1c" :answer/id #uuid "493e3c85-b25e-53b6-a08c-4fea9dba4c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35b1eb42-ba69-53f4-81c2-c8740d0d9806" :answer/id #uuid "35b1eb42-ba69-53f4-81c2-c8740d0d9806" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2561f127-b662-5797-b919-80264e333b26" :answer/id #uuid "2561f127-b662-5797-b919-80264e333b26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c48feefc-15c4-5bef-ac32-e7d9d07bb0ce" :answer/id #uuid "c48feefc-15c4-5bef-ac32-e7d9d07bb0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d04f3cfc-1715-5df0-995f-34492b52003c" :answer/id #uuid "d04f3cfc-1715-5df0-995f-34492b52003c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186078394 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-44ffb250-1ebe-5832-a06b-038dd7ff73b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-44ffb250-1ebe-5832-a06b-038dd7ff73b2" :question/id #uuid "44ffb250-1ebe-5832-a06b-038dd7ff73b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122171" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bff27a71fc8421d51e69a677260f60a1e421c09fe3969f70d4c07bf1ac58576.png)\n\nFind the tangent of $∠P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the definition of tangent: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡P=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{QR}{PQ}=\\frac{QR}{3.5}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing length $QR.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}QR & =\\sqrt{P{R}^{2}-P{Q}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{12.5}^{2}-{3.5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{156.25-12.25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡P & =\\frac{QR}{3.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-518b1e5c-6389-594b-b333-90ba109eabdc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-518b1e5c-6389-594b-b333-90ba109eabdc" :answer-field/id #uuid "518b1e5c-6389-594b-b333-90ba109eabdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f46bc196-b847-5053-8f6e-796c26a26b99" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dcdc4442-a9d9-5305-bc8b-adc1a7389cb8" "answer-9a5b3adb-f36e-546f-90c5-4151e04b2960" "answer-f46bc196-b847-5053-8f6e-796c26a26b99" "answer-b43265d8-cc49-526f-8e22-5651c777ca5c" "answer-24c3606f-796c-5b0b-8a50-19ba888da79b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcdc4442-a9d9-5305-bc8b-adc1a7389cb8" :answer/id #uuid "dcdc4442-a9d9-5305-bc8b-adc1a7389cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a5b3adb-f36e-546f-90c5-4151e04b2960" :answer/id #uuid "9a5b3adb-f36e-546f-90c5-4151e04b2960" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f46bc196-b847-5053-8f6e-796c26a26b99" :answer/id #uuid "f46bc196-b847-5053-8f6e-796c26a26b99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b43265d8-cc49-526f-8e22-5651c777ca5c" 